From fe2019f22f173c334a0550eff7f293f88656fe8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:39:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: a configured HDMI output that is not there follows
 the display too

Since "the audio output follows the display when the configured one has
none", the engine uses the only HDMI output with a display in place of
a configured one that the driver says has none. A configured output
that is not there at all was left as it was.

That is the state of a laptop started with its dedicated graphics
only, when the output of its integrated graphics was chosen in an
earlier start (seen in a report of 2026-10-17: the setting on
"hdmi:CARD=PCH,DEV=0", which did not exist in that start, the TV on
the first HDMI output of the NVIDIA graphics). Kodi validated the
setting when the engine started (ValidateOutputDevices()), in memory
and to the analog output of the same card, the laptop's own sound.
Every new stream loads the settings again without that validation, and
the engine tried the output that is not there, then the default
device, for which no format could be set up: no sink, and the video
played without sound.

A configured output that is not there now counts as an output without
a display when its name says that it is an HDMI or DisplayPort one
(the ALSA sink names those "hdmi:..."): with exactly one output of the
driver with a display, that one is used. With several displays the
choice stays with the user, and with none the output that was followed
to stays in use while it is there, as for an output without a display.
A configured output that is not there and is no display output (a USB
sound card that was unplugged) is left to Kodi's validation, as
before. The setting is not changed: when the configured output is
there again, it is used again.

The decision is a function of its own, ActiveAE::INTERNAL::
FollowedDisplayOutput(), with a test (TestActiveAEFollowDisplay) that
also holds the rules of before. The log says when the configured
output is not there, instead of that it has no display.
